# Fluorescence buffer-gas cooling cell, true 3D, 23K neon DSMC.
# Mirrors cases/takahashi-3d/in.he_takahashi_3d_scoping's structure.
#
# Geometry: cell_fluor3d.surf, generated by gen_fluor3d.py from the CAD
# (fluorescence_cooling_cell_installed.step). Screw holes plugged, only the
# 3 functional ports remain:
#   type 1 = generic 23K wall
#   type 2 = buffer gas inlet -- SEALED (emit/surf mass-flow source), not an
#            open hole. Modeling choice: gas is injected as if from the end
#            of a feed line plugged into the real 1.588mm port, matching the
#            emit/surf-on-sealed-wall convention both existing cases use.
#            Verify this matches your actual gas feed hardware.
#   type 3 = molecule inlet channel (2.54mm, OPEN to exterior) -- SPARTA
#            does not track molecules/ions (that's the Julia tracer, via the
#            frozen Ne field); this is tagged only so its Ne flux/leakage
#            can be measured separately if useful.
#   type 4 = molecule outlet channel (3.175mm, OPEN to exterior) -- same.
#
# Species: ne.species/ne.vss, standard literature VHS parameters (Bird 1994
# Table A1: d=2.79e-10m, omega=0.66, Tref=273.15K) -- NOT the simplified
# hard-sphere convention he.species/he.vss uses, by request, for physical
# accuracy at 23K rather than methodological consistency with the He cases.
#
# NOTE ON IONS: BaF+ at 500 eV is NOT represented anywhere in this deck.
# SPARTA here only simulates the neutral Ne buffer gas. The existing Julia
# tracer's mean-speed elastic-collision approximation assumes near-thermal
# species entrained by the gas flow -- a 500 eV ion thermalizing in 23K Ne
# is an ion-stopping/energy-loss problem (many collisions, large fractional
# energy loss each), not something that tracer models correctly. That needs
# a separate stopping-power/energy-loss treatment before trusting any BaF+
# trajectory or stopping-distance result. See project discussion -- flagged,
# not implemented here.
#
# TODO before a real run (needs domain knowledge this pass didn't have):
#   - create_box / region gas bounds below are a generous placeholder, not
#     derived from your actual downstream vacuum chamber or pumping setup.
#   - create_grid is a single flat level; the existing cases use nested 2:1
#     refinement bands sized to the local mean free path (see gen_b5.py's
#     nonface() checks and in.he_b5_mflow's region levelN blocks). This
#     geometry's ports (1.588/2.54/3.175mm) likely need similar treatment,
#     and the mean free path at 23K neon differs from the He cases' 4K --
#     re-derive cell sizing, don't reuse their numbers.
#   - MDOT/FILLN/FNUM/DT/STEPS: pass with -var, same as tools/run_helium.sh.
#   - Buffer gas inlet cap placement (30.48,25.400,0.5mm depth -- see
#     gen_fluor3d.py's GAS_INLET_CAP_DEPTH_MM) is a modeling assumption,
#     not a CAD feature -- confirm it's a reasonable stand-in for the real
#     feed line before trusting absolute flow-field numbers near that port.

variable    SEED index 8675309
variable    WEIGHT index radius
seed        ${SEED}
units       si
dimension   3
boundary    o o o
global      gridcut 0.0
create_box  0.005 0.200 -0.020 0.070 -0.030 0.080
create_grid 60 27 33
balance_grid rcb cell
global      mem/limit 1900
species     ne.species Ne
mixture     negas Ne nrho 1.0e22 temp 23.0
mixture     fillgas Ne nrho ${FILLN} temp 23.0
global      fnum ${FNUM}
collide     vss negas ne.vss
read_surf   cell_fluor3d.surf type group cellwalls clip
surf_collide walls diffuse 23.0 1.0
surf_modify cellwalls collide walls
group       gasinlet surf type 2
group       moleculein surf type 3
group       moleculeout surf type 4
region      gas block 0.031 0.082 0.001 0.043 -0.005 0.039
create_particles fillgas n 0 region gas
balance_grid rcb part
fix         bal balance 5000 1.1 rcb time
global      particle/reorder 100
fix         src emit/surf negas gasinlet normal yes mflow ${MDOT} 23.0
compute     cmi surf moleculein negas nflux norm flow
fix         ami ave/surf moleculein 10 100 1000 c_cmi[1]
dump        dmi surf moleculein 1000 moleculein.out id f_ami
compute     cmo surf moleculeout negas nflux norm flow
fix         amo ave/surf moleculeout 10 100 1000 c_cmo[1]
dump        dmo surf moleculeout 1000 moleculeout.out id f_amo
compute     cg grid all negas nrho u v w
compute     tg thermal/grid all negas temp
fix         ag ave/grid all 10 2000 20000 c_cg[*] c_tg[*]
dump        gd grid all 20000 field.grid id xc yc zc xlo ylo zlo xhi yhi zhi f_ag[*]
stats       5000
stats_style step cpu np nattempt ncoll f_src[1] f_src[2]
stats_modify flush yes
timestep    ${DT}
run         ${STEPS}
